     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. The dose looks like it may be a mistake, so please check it first.\n\n**Amlodipine 50 mg once daily is 5 times the usual maximum.** For adults, amlodipine is normally dosed at 2.5\u201310 mg once daily, and 10 mg/day is the maximum. At 50 mg, the patient could develop severe low blood pressure, reflex tachycardia, and swelling. An overdose can be hard to reverse because amlodipine stays in the body for a long time (half-life of about 30\u201350 hours).\n\nA common mix-up is **5 mg**, the usual starting dose, being written as 50 mg.\n\nPlease reply with one of these:\n- **The corrected dose** (for example, 5 mg or 10 mg once daily), and I'll enter it right away.\n- **Confirmation that 50 mg is intended**, with the clinical reason. I'd strongly recommend checking with a pharmacist first. If you still want it entered, I'll attach a note to the order recording that the dose was confirmed as above the maximum."
      }
     ],
