       "type": "text",
       "text": "I've entered the order as written: **amlodipine 50 mg by mouth, once daily (Order ID: ORD-0001).**\n\nI added a note to the order saying the dose is 5 times the usual maximum of 10 mg/day, that you confirmed it, and that no clinical reason was given. The note also recommends a pharmacist check it before it's dispensed.\n\n**Please double-check this one more time.** I don't know of any approved use for 50 mg/day. Because amlodipine stays in the body so long, a dose this high could cause severe low blood pressure that lasts for days.\n\n**If you meant 5 mg,** tell me and I'll enter a corrected order. The 50 mg order (ORD-0001) would need to be cancelled in the system. I can't cancel orders with the tools I have.\n\n**If 50 mg is intended,** consider adding the clinical reason to the chart, and arrange extra blood pressure and heart rate monitoring."
